However, I plan on making the warmage class a little bit weaker than
the wizard in some ways.

First, I plan on making it so that a warmage can only advance attack
spells up to expert.  The rest of the spellcasting skills permenantly
stay at unskilled.  Warmages have a single focus on spellcasting that
does damage.  (I have also been thinking of giving a penalty to
warmages not casting an attack spell, or having the quest artifact
prohibit the use of non-attack spells, or other such nerfs).

Second, I am not giving a warmage hungerless casting.

Third, the warmage has much weaker gear, as you can see above, than
the wizard.

However, the warmage will have one advantage, that armor won't affect
their spellcasting nearly as much.  Warmages have been specially
trained on how to cast spells through their armor.


